WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:06.359
Marvel’s Daredevil on Netflix looks set
to be the new superhero series to beat, giving

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:10.250
Arrow and The Flash quite a run for their
vigilante money.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:16.250
Forget 2003’s Daredevil movie starring Ben
Affleck, which mixed po-faced melodrama with

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.010
cheesy cartoony elements.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:24.000
This new Daredevil series is an entirely different
beast and takes Marvel into darker, grittier

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.040
territory than we’ve seen before while still
firmly locating the world of our new small-screen

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.469
superhero within the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:32.469 --> 00:00:37.870
With 13 episodes of about 50 minutes each
to play with, Daredevil takes an enjoyably

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:44.629
slow-build approach to introducing us to Matt
Murdock, a brilliant blind lawyer by day and

00:00:44.629 --> 00:00:47.039
a violent masked vigilante by night.

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:52.079
Through a series of flashbacks cleverly integrated
into Murdock’s present-day story, we find

00:00:52.079 --> 00:00:56.999
out how he came to be a street-level hero
with enhanced senses, a vigilante on a mission

00:00:56.999 --> 00:00:58.310
to save his city.

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:02.219
The show has a feeling of realism that’s
due to many things: there’s the performances

00:01:02.219 --> 00:01:06.930
of the actors themselves, there’s the Hell’s
Kitchen setting and New York filming locations,

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:11.070
there’s how the fight scenes are staged,
and there’s the way the writers gradually

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.230
build up the layers of these characters and
their stories.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:19.760
And then there’s the show’s darkness,
both in terms of its appearance and its attitude.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.230
Even the series’ opening credits look like
they’re dripping blood.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:27.790
Murdock lives in the deliberately murky-looking
neighbourhood of Hell’s Kitchen in a New

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:31.260
York City still dealing with the aftermath
of the Avengers’ first assembly.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:36.880
There’s a feeling of film noir in the playful
use of shadows in the show, and a distinct

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.950
air of 1970s American movies like Taxi Driver
in the its grounded grittiness.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:47.820
And that edginess extends to the script and
its unflinching commitment not to shy away

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.700
from the intense and, at times, brutal nature
of Murdock’s story.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:56.820
From what I’ve seen of the series so far,
Murdock’s Daredevil doesn’t shrink from

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.850
violence or meting out justice as he feels
fit.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:04.480
Imagine the Oliver Queen we met in Season
1 of Arrow on steroids!

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:09.819
Among those who deserve credit for Daredevil’s
quite daring tone are executive producer Drew

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:14.819
Goddard, who very much sets the mood with
his writing on the first two episodes, showrunner

00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:18.099
Steven DeKnight, and the series’ cinematographer
Matthew Lloyd.

00:02:18.099 --> 00:02:24.819
As for the cast, Charlie Cox puts in a pitch-perfect
performance as both super-smart and super-charming

00:02:24.819 --> 00:02:31.150
lawyer Matt Murdock, and his kick-ass, power-punching
alter-ego Daredevil, whose initial black costume

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.430
fits well with the show’s dark themes.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:38.780
Elden Henson brings a real likeability to
Foggy, who’s Murdock’s friend and partner-in-law,

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:43.969
and he also adds a nice line in humour, throwing
some light among the show’s shadows.

00:02:43.969 --> 00:02:48.920
Plus, there’s a lovely, natural chemistry
between Henson’s Foggy and True Blood star

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:52.639
Deborah Ann Woll, who plays their first client,
Karen Page.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:58.139
As nurse Claire Temple, Rosario Dawson’s
time on the show is certainly off to an interesting

00:02:58.139 --> 00:02:59.139
start.

00:02:59.139 --> 00:03:03.969
And Vincent D’Onofrio’s turn as shadowy
businessman Wilson Fisk is nicely understated,

00:03:03.969 --> 00:03:06.340
with an ever-present hint of danger.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:10.980
While Toby Leonard Moore hits all the right
notes as Fisk’s right-hand man, Wesley.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.800
And Vondie Curtis-Hall is totally convincing
as old-fashioned newspaper journalist Ben,

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.290
who wants to unearth stories that make a difference.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:22.910
And if it’s action you’re after, you certainly
won’t be disappointed with Daredevil.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:28.609
There are plenty of amazing fight scenes,
which mix down-and-dirty brawling with martial

00:03:28.609 --> 00:03:30.290
arts influences to great effect.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:35.139
The show’s stunt team, including stunt and
fight co-ordinator Philip J Silvera, really

00:03:35.139 --> 00:03:37.999
have done a superb job.

00:03:37.999 --> 00:03:42.810
Oh, and listen out for the sound during those
fights – it's bone-crunchingly intense!

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:47.829
After watching the first five episodes of
Daredevil, I cannot wait to watch the rest!

00:03:47.829 --> 00:03:52.639
And I’m now even more excited to see the
other street-level hero series that Marvel’s

00:03:52.639 --> 00:03:59.400
got up its sleeve, including AKA Jessica Jones,
Iron Fist, and Luke Cage; all of whose main

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.840
characters will team up with Daredevil in
The Defenders.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.939
Lots to look forward to!

00:04:04.939 --> 00:04:10.919
So, to sum up: Daredevil is a delectably dark
dive into the world of Marvel’s popular

00:04:10.919 --> 00:04:12.499
street-level hero.

00:04:12.499 --> 00:04:17.919
Combining an incredible cast and awesome stunts
with a smart slow-burn script, the series

00:04:17.919 --> 00:04:21.639
shows that justice can be both blind and bloody.

00:04:21.639 --> 00:04:24.750
Daredevil gets 4.5 out of 5 Flicks.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:28.919
